Implements the first track of the work split: the graph structure and the
decision brain, testable end to end on stubs.

- state.py: AgentState per contract 1, plus four additive HITL/tracing fields
  (issue_title, issue_body, approved, supervisor_log) documented in CONTRACTS.md
- guardrail: rejects empty input, non-GitHub URLs, and reserved github.com paths
- fetch: three failure paths — RepoNotFound, tool error, and success-but-empty
- supervisor: eligibility computed in code, ordering decided by the LLM, with a
  deterministic fallback when the LLM is unavailable and validation of every
  model choice before it can route
- build: three conditional edges, the agent loop, MemorySaver checkpointer and
  interrupt_before=["publish"] for human approval
- stubs.py: temporary fakes of track-2 pieces, with a deletion checklist
- llm.py: provider factory (anthropic/openai/google) switched by env var
- scripts: 6 graph scenarios + 11 supervisor logic checks, all passing without
  an API key or network access
- HANDOFF.md: signatures, contract changes and constraints for track 2

